  "description": "Code Kernel '26 | Decode → Build → Prove An online national problem-solving competition by X-Kernel , the student-led technical and innovation club of Gokaraju Rangaraju Institute of Engineering and Technology (GRIET), Hyderabad. Tentative dates: 21 October – 31 October 2026 Registrations close: 20 October 2026 Mode: Online Team size: 1 to 4 students Format: Decode → Build → Prove What it is Students enter in teams of 1 to 4. Each team takes one real problem through three stages in order. This is not a pitch contest and not a prototype-only hackathon. The work has to hold up when the test changes. Rounds Round 1: Decode (21–24 Oct). Understand the real problem before writing a solution: root cause, people affected, existing limits, and whether your approach can work. Teams submit their solution approach. Round 2: Build (25–29 Oct). Shortlisted teams build a practical response, not a slide. It can be software, AI/ML, web or mobile, automation, data, a technical or business solution, a hardware simulation, or a proof of concept. Submit a GitHub repo, demo video and deployed link. Round 3: Prove (30–31 Oct). Show it still works when the test changes, with unseen checks, extra constraints, new test cases, a live demo and questions from the judges. Problems Each problem is framed as problem, context, constraints and expected outcome. Sponsor partners may contribute problem statements. Eligibility Open to students from any college and branch across India Teams of 1 to 4 Fully online participation Community Join our participant Discord for updates, announcements and help: https://discord.gg/cxNq7SRqK Note: Dates are tentative and may change slightly. Existing registrations remain valid.",
