    "details": "<p><strong>Code Kernel '26 | Decode &rarr; Build &rarr; Prove</strong></p>\n<p>An online national problem-solving competition by <strong>X-Kernel</strong>, the student-led technical and innovation club of Gokaraju Rangaraju Institute of Engineering and Technology (GRIET), Hyderabad.</p>\n<p><strong>Tentative dates:</strong> 21 October &ndash; 31 October 2026<br /><strong>Registrations close:</strong> 20 October 2026<br /><strong>Mode:</strong> Online<br /><strong>Team size:</strong> 1 to 4 students<br /><strong>Format:</strong> Decode &rarr; Build &rarr; Prove</p>\n<p><strong>What it is</strong><br />Students enter in teams of 1 to 4. Each team takes one real problem through three stages in order. This is not a pitch contest and not a prototype-only hackathon. The work has to hold up when the test changes.</p>\n<p><strong>Rounds</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Round 1: Decode (21&ndash;24 Oct).</strong> Understand the real problem before writing a solution: root cause, people affected, existing limits, and whether your approach can work. Teams submit their solution approach.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 2: Build (25&ndash;29 Oct).</strong> Shortlisted teams build a practical response, not a slide. It can be software, AI/ML, web or mobile, automation, data, a technical or business solution, a hardware simulation, or a proof of concept. Submit a GitHub repo, demo video and deployed link.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 3: Prove (30&ndash;31 Oct).</strong> Show it still works when the test changes, with unseen checks, extra constraints, new test cases, a live demo and questions from the judges.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Problems</strong><br />Each problem is framed as problem, context, constraints and expected outcome. Sponsor partners may contribute problem statements.</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to students from any college and branch across India</li>\n<li>Teams of 1 to 4</li>\n<li>Fully online participation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Community</strong><br />Join our participant Discord for updates, announcements and help: https://discord.gg/cxNq7SRqK</p>\n<p><em>Note: Dates are tentative and may change slightly. Existing registrations remain valid.</em></p>",
